<title>FRANCE: Chirac committed to Maastricht criteria - Blair.</title>
<headline>Chirac committed to Maastricht criteria - Blair.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British opposition leader Tony Blair said on Friday French President Jacques Chirac assured him France would stick to the criteria for joining a European single currency defined in the Maastricth treaty.</p>
<p>Asked whether he was concerned &quot;fudging&quot; of the criteria would weaken a single currency, Blair said &quot;Well, President Chirac gave a very strong commitment to maintaining the criteria in the Maastricht treaty as did (Prime Minister Alain) Juppe earlier.&quot;</p>
<p>Blair was speaking to reporters after a meeting with the French president in Paris. He met Juppe earlier on Friday.</p>
</text>
